@page "/integration-overview"

<PageTitle>Integration Overview - OperationsFlow</PageTitle>

<div class="operations-dashboard integration-overview-page">
    <PageIntro Eyebrow="Production Planning"
               Title="Microsoft 365 / Integration Overview"
               Subtitle="A production-aware overview of how OperationsFlow could connect to Microsoft 365, SharePoint, Teams, Outlook, reporting exports, and external business systems.">
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="deployment-overview">Deployment Overview</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="technical-overview">Technical Overview</a>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="portfolio-hub">Portfolio Hub</a>
    </PageIntro>

    <div class="page-purpose-note">
        <strong>Purpose:</strong> use this page to show the realistic integration path for OperationsFlow. The current prototype is local and self-contained, but the workflow model is designed so records, documents, reminders, reports, and activity history could later connect to Microsoft 365 and other business systems.
    </div>

    <section class="kpi-grid">
        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Current State</span>
            <strong>Local</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Prototype data and demo workflow</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Main Target</span>
            <strong>M365</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">SharePoint / Teams / Outlook</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Reporting Path</span>
            <strong>Exports</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">CSV / Excel / Power BI-ready data</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Integration Style</span>
            <strong>Phased</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Start small before full sync</span>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="summary-grid integration-intro-grid">
        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Integration Summary</h2>
                    <p>How the current prototype could connect to real business tools.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="integration-copy">
                OperationsFlow is currently a local Blazor/.NET prototype. In a production version, the same workflow
                records could connect to Microsoft 365 so documents are stored in SharePoint, reminders are sent through
                Teams or Outlook, reports can be exported for management review, and activity history can support audit
                and follow-up conversations.
            </p>

            <ul class="action-list">
                <li>Keep OperationsFlow as the workflow and review layer.</li>
                <li>Use SharePoint for controlled document storage and file links.</li>
                <li>Use Teams or Outlook for due-soon, overdue, and owner notifications.</li>
                <li>Export structured data for Excel, Power BI, or management reporting.</li>
                <li>Add API or scheduled sync only after core workflow rules are stable.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Prototype Boundary</h2>
                    <p>What is planned, not currently live.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="integration-boundary-highlight">
                <span>Prototype boundary</span>
                <strong>No live Microsoft 365 integration yet</strong>
                <p>
                    The current version demonstrates the workflow model and integration-ready structure. It does not yet
                    connect to live SharePoint libraries, Teams messages, Outlook emails, Microsoft Lists, Power BI,
                    accounting systems, or production APIs.
                </p>
            </div>

            <ol class="action-list">
                <li>Confirm which workflow should be integrated first.</li>
                <li>Confirm the real source of truth for each record type.</li>
                <li>Connect documents before adding automated notifications.</li>
                <li>Add reporting exports before complex two-way sync.</li>
            </ol>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="integration-card-grid">
        @foreach (var integration in IntegrationTargets)
        {
            <article class="integration-card">
                <div class="integration-card-header">
                    <span>@integration.Number</span>
                    <div>
                        <p class="eyebrow">@integration.Category</p>
                        <h2>@integration.Title</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <p>@integration.Description</p>

                <div class="integration-state-pair">
                    <div>
                        <span>Current Prototype</span>
                        <strong>@integration.CurrentState</strong>
                    </div>

                    <div>
                        <span>Production Upgrade</span>
                        <strong>@integration.ProductionUpgrade</strong>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </article>
        }
    </section>

    <section class="report-card">
        <div class="panel-header">
            <div>
                <h2>Integration Readiness Matrix</h2>
                <p>How each major integration would support the workflow.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <table class="report-table integration-matrix-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Integration</th>
                    <th>Business Purpose</th>
                    <th>OperationsFlow Use</th>
                    <th>Recommended Phase</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var row in IntegrationMatrix)
                {
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>@row.Integration</strong></td>
                        <td>@row.BusinessPurpose</td>
                        <td>@row.OperationsFlowUse</td>
                        <td><span class="@row.BadgeClass">@row.Phase</span></td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>

    <section class="summary-grid">
        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Phased Integration Plan</h2>
                    <p>The safest way to connect a prototype to real business systems.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <ol class="demo-step-list integration-phase-list">
                <li>
                    <strong>Start with exports</strong>
                    <span>Export reports or CSV files so managers can review data before live system integration.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Add document links</strong>
                    <span>Connect records to SharePoint document locations without moving the whole workflow into SharePoint immediately.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Add owner notifications</strong>
                    <span>Send overdue and due-soon notifications through Teams or Outlook after owner/status rules are confirmed.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Add authentication and roles</strong>
                    <span>Use Microsoft identity or another provider so workflow changes are tied to real users.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Add API or scheduled sync</strong>
                    <span>Only introduce two-way integration after records, ownership, statuses, and data rules are stable.</span>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Integration Risks</h2>
                    <p>What needs to be controlled before live sync.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="integration-risk-grid">
                @foreach (var risk in IntegrationRisks)
                {
                    <article>
                        <span>@risk.Label</span>
                        <strong>@risk.Title</strong>
                        <p>@risk.Description</p>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="report-card">
        <div class="panel-header">
            <div>
                <h2>Microsoft 365 Workflow Map</h2>
                <p>Where Microsoft 365 tools would fit around the OperationsFlow workflow.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <table class="report-table m365-workflow-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Workflow Need</th>
                    <th>Microsoft 365 Tool</th>
                    <th>Example Use</th>
                    <th>Review Value</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var row in Microsoft365Map)
                {
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>@row.WorkflowNeed</strong></td>
                        <td><span class="@row.BadgeClass">@row.Tool</span></td>
                        <td>@row.ExampleUse</td>
                        <td>@row.ReviewValue</td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>

    <section class="summary-grid">
        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Data Flow After Integration</h2>
                    <p>How information would move through a production version.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <ol class="demo-step-list integration-data-flow">
                <li>
                    <strong>Record is created</strong>
                    <span>A corrective action, document intake item, risk review, training issue, or work order is entered into OperationsFlow.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Owner and due date are assigned</strong>
                    <span>The record becomes visible in workload, reminders, reports, data quality, and review pages.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Document link is attached</strong>
                    <span>If evidence or controlled documents are required, the record links to SharePoint or another approved storage location.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Notification is sent</strong>
                    <span>Teams or Outlook reminds the owner before due dates or escalates overdue work.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Report or review pack is exported</strong>
                    <span>Management can review structured outputs without manually rebuilding the same summary in spreadsheets.</span>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>What This Proves</h2>
                    <p>The portfolio value of integration thinking.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="integration-proof-grid">
                @foreach (var proof in ProofItems)
                {
                    <article>
                        <span>@proof.Label</span>
                        <strong>@proof.Title</strong>
                        <p>@proof.Description</p>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="report-card integration-summary-card">
        <div class="panel-header">
            <div>
                <h2>Integration Overview Summary</h2>
                <p>A short explanation for reviewers.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="integration-summary-copy">
            <p>
                OperationsFlow is not currently connected to live Microsoft 365 services. The current version is a local
                workflow prototype that demonstrates how business records, ownership, statuses, due dates, notes,
                reporting views, reminders, and activity history could work before live integrations are added.
            </p>

            <p>
                The most realistic production path would be phased: begin with report exports, add SharePoint document
                links, add Teams or Outlook notifications, connect authentication and roles, then add API or scheduled
                sync once the workflow rules are stable. This keeps the system low-risk while still showing a clear path
                from local portfolio prototype to integrated internal business tool.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>

@code {
